{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 11, :comments [{:quotes [{:he "ותמלא הארץ", :translit "u't'malei ha'aretz", :gloss "and the earth was filled"} {:he "ותמלא הארץ אתם", :translit "u't'malei ha'aretz otam", :gloss "and the earth was filled with them"}], :mechanisms [{:kind :masorah, :count 2, :occurrences ["ותמלא הארץ" "ותמלא הארץ אתם"]}], :frame {:text "The phrase ותמלא הארץ appears exactly twice in Scripture — here in Genesis 6:11 (ותמלא הארץ חמס) and in Genesis 6:13 (ותמלא הארץ אתם) — forming a standard Masoretah pair (Shemuel ha-Naqdan, Siman 44). The flood-generation's extraordinary fertility is described as women bearing multiple children per pregnancy (Sanhedrin 108b–109a). Their practice of violence extended to ingenious theft: when someone deposited valuables for safekeeping, the depositary buried them with fragrant balsam as a marker, then returned at night to steal the deposit (Sanhedrian 108b).", :sources ["Sanhedrin 108b" "Sanhedrin 109a"]}} {:quotes [{:he "חמם", :translit "chamas", :gloss "violence"} {:he "מי נח", :translit "mei Noach", :gloss "waters of Noah"} {:he "גיהנם", :translit "geihinnom", :gloss "Gehenna"}], :mechanisms [{:kind :gematria, :a "חמם", :b "מי נח"} {:kind :gematria, :a "חמם", :b "גיהנם"}], :frame {:text "The phrase מי נח appears in Isaiah 54:9, where God swears never again to bring the waters of Noah over the earth. The wicked of the generation were punished with boiling waters in Gehenna (Eikhah Rabbah 1:1).", :sources ["Isaiah 54:9" "Eikhah Rabbah 1:1"]}}], :arithmetic [{:kind :masorah, :count 2, :occurrences ["ותמלא הארץ" "ותמלא הארץ אתם"], :by :selah, :located [{:phrase "ותמלא הארץ", :refs ["Genesis 6:11" "Exodus 1:7" "2 Kings 3:20" "Ezekiel 9:9"], :n 4, :lens :exact} {:phrase "ותמלא הארץ אתם", :refs ["Exodus 1:7"], :n 1, :lens :exact}]} {:kind :gematria, :a "חמם", :a-value 88, :b "מי נח", :b-value 108, :lens :standard, :by :selah, :equal? false} {:kind :gematria, :a "חמם", :a-value 88, :b "גיהנם", :b-value 108, :lens :standard, :by :selah